From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: server: on a shared prefix, SYSTEM's token is elevated

An elevated program runs as SYSTEM (ADR 0012), and SYSTEM's token had
elevation type Limited, so TokenElevation said it was not elevated. The .NET
SDK's installer (WiX Burn) refused to work from its elevated engine and
failed with 0x8000ffff. Type Full: kernelbase, shell32 and the loader already
treat it as elevated, and a requireAdministrator program the broker starts
keeps SYSTEM's token rather than Wine's generic administrator's.

--- a/server/process.c
+++ b/server/process.c
@@ -722,12 +722,15 @@
             /* The user's hive has to exist before anything touches HKCU, and
              * this is the first moment we know which user that is. */
             sg_ensure_user_hive( process->peer_uid );
-            /* Stained Glass OS (D17): only SYSTEM has a linked administrator
-             * token; a standard user's elevation type is Default, as on
-             * Windows, and elevation goes through the broker (ADR 0012). */
+            /* Stained Glass OS (D17): SYSTEM is elevated -- what an elevated
+             * program runs as (TokenElevation says so: the .NET SDK's
+             * installer refused to install from an engine that was "not
+             * running with elevated privileges"); a standard user's elevation
+             * type is Default, as on Windows, and elevation goes through the
+             * broker (ADR 0012). */
             process->token = token_create_for_uid( TRUE, -1,
                                                    (!process->peer_uid || process->peer_uid == sg_system_prefix_uid)
-                                                   ? TokenElevationTypeLimited : TokenElevationTypeDefault,
+                                                   ? TokenElevationTypeFull : TokenElevationTypeDefault,
                                                    default_session_id, process->peer_uid );
         }
         else
